{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate zero access safety barriers for apex predators in all licensed zoos",
        "additional_details": "Many zoos rely on open-air platforms and wire fencing designed only for standard visitor behaviour. We feel these boundaries fail to prevent individuals from bypassing containment to enter dangerous habitats. This statutory requirement could eliminate unauthorised public entry, safeguard emergency first-responders from severe operational trauma, and protect the safety of animals involved.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to amend the Zoo Licensing Act 1981 and the Standards of Modern Zoo Practice to mandate that facilities keeping Category 1 Dangerous Wild Animals (Schedule 1, Dangerous Wild Animals Act 1976) install unclimbable glass barriers or impassable stand-off zones.",
